From: grislux55 <jebchou.hg@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: usb: add GPIO based VBUS over-current protection

Describe a USB port power switch whose fault flag is wired to a GPIO and
whose VBUS regulator the operating system switches off while the flag
reports over-current.

Signed-off-by: grislux55 <jebchou.hg@gmail.com>
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/usb-vbus-oc-gpio.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/usb/usb-vbus-oc-gpio.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: USB VBUS over-current protection through a GPIO fault flag
+
+maintainers:
+  - grislux55 <jebchou.hg@gmail.com>
+
+description:
+  A USB port power switch that reports over-current on a fault flag line. The
+  operating system switches VBUS off while the flag is asserted and back on
+  once it clears. The node is the only consumer of the VBUS regulator, so the
+  host controller node carries no vbus-supply.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: usb-vbus-oc-gpio
+
+  overcurrent-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: Fault flag of the power switch, asserted on over-current.
+
+  vbus-supply:
+    description: Regulator that switches VBUS of the port.
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - overcurrent-gpios
+  - vbus-supply
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
+
+    usb-vbus-oc {
+        compatible = "usb-vbus-oc-gpio";
+        overcurrent-gpios = <&gpio 21 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+        vbus-supply = <&reg_usb_vbus>;
+    };
